<title>USA: Lear says GM strike cuts Q4 by $0.10/shr.</title>
<headline>Lear says GM strike cuts Q4 by $0.10/shr.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lear Corp said on Tuesday its fourth quarter earnings will be cut by about $0.10 a share due to recent union work stoppages at General Motors Corp production facilities.</p>
<p>Lear is the world's largest independent supplier of automotive interior systems. It had 1995 sales of $4.7 billion.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
